{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>it shall be washed in a holy place.</b> Scripture was stringent regarding blood absorbed in a garment, requiring that it be done where it was prior to the spattering, so that it not go outside the hangings. And it says, \"but the earthen vessel in which it was boiled shall be broken\" (Leviticus 6:21), and it too is broken in a holy place and the sherds remain absorbed in their place, and no purging and rinsing is done with it at all. And likewise the purging and rinsing in a bronze vessel is done in a holy place, for all the verses are drawn back to \"a holy place\" that it mentioned."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:08.541192536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}